{"end_exclusive":2463432,"entries":[{"attestation_cbor_b32":"","entry_cbor_b32":"","entry_hash_b32":"quzqrplqfultmmku5efrp4pnghwqpf37rimscveyxbonqxnsk33a","entry_kind":"attestation","leaf_index":2463431}],"max_per_call":256,"note":"RFC 6962 get-entries. leaf_index is global and append-only, and entry i is the preimage of leaf i in /v1/log/sth: re-hash entry_cbor_b32 with blake3 and it equals entry_hash_b32, which /v1/log/inclusion proves is committed under the STH. Enumerate to audit the log rather than only proving inclusion of a cid you already hold. Four kinds of entry: `attestation` (CBOR of a signed emem_fact::Attestation), `emem.memory_write.v1` (a CBOR map naming a memory note by path, file_cid and content_blake3, with the author's key and signature), `emem.memory_supersede.v1` and `emem.memory_delete.v1` (a supersede or a delete, with the author's key and signature). attestation_cbor_b32 is the legacy name of entry_cbor_b32 and holds the same bytes for both kinds.","returned":1,"spec":"https://emem.dev/spec.md#transparency-log","start":2463431,"summary":false,"truncated":false}